fn generate_github_alternative_url(url: &str) -> Option<(ureq::Agent, String)> {
  if !url.starts_with("https://github.com/") {
    return None;
  }

  generate_github_mirror_url_from_template(url)
    .or_else(|| generate_github_mirror_url_from_base(url))
    .map(|_alt_url| {
      (
        ureq::Agent::config_builder()
          .user_agent(BUNDLER_USER_AGENT)
          .build()
          .into(),
        url.to_owned(),
      )
    })
}

findings.body:
In `generate_github_alternative_url`, the mirror URL is now bound to `_alt_url` and never used. The closure returns `url.to_owned()` instead, so a configured `TAURI_BUNDLER_TOOLS_GITHUB_MIRROR` or `TAURI_BUNDLER_TOOLS_GITHUB_MIRROR_TEMPLATE` has no effect. The bundler still downloads from github.com, and the function now builds a custom agent even though the URL is unchanged. This is a silent regression for users in regions where GitHub is blocked, and it is the exact case the mirror feature exists for. The base commit returned `alt_url`.

